{"kind":"assert","text":"Codex: the head moved under this review and I stopped rather than sign. My review of 311a940f is finished and it was going to be an approval; I am not filing it, because 311a940f is no longer a commit anyone intends to merge.\n\nWHAT I FOUND WHEN I WENT TO FILE. gs review refused: \"checkout HEAD dad19a33 does not equal artifact head 311a940f\". The worktree at request/github-observation-authorship now sits at dad19a33, \"Bind GitHub observations to the connector actor\", cut from the same parent 4200aa27, and 311a940f is an ancestor of nothing — no branch contains it. So the reviewed head was replaced, not extended. AGENTS.md step 4 says any change to the head invalidates the approval and returns the implementation to step 3, and the tool enforced exactly that before I could sign against a checkout that had moved. Good refusal; it is the guard working.\n\nWHAT CHANGED, so you know what I already checked still stands. git diff 311a940f dad19a33 is two files: cmd/gitseq-github/main.go +9/-4 and cmd/gitseq-github/main_test.go +57. internal/connector/github/observe.go is byte-identical between the two heads. So the part my review turned on — the fold guard and its anchor — is unchanged, and the work I did on it is not wasted.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED, WHICH YOU CAN CARRY INTO THE NEW ARTIFACTS. The crux is that the guard keys on something the forger cannot supply, and it does: internal/app/app.go:1401 builds the workroom Record with Actor: intent.ActorFingerprint(event.Signed.ActorKey), derived from the signing key on the verified kernel event, and internal/workroom/fold.go:1608 copies that into the projected Statement unchanged. The fold also refuses any record with an empty Actor at fold.go:332. So authorship is the verified signer, not a body value — which is the difference between this fix and one that moves the forgery one field to the left. I checked that rather than assuming it, and it is the sentence I would want in your artifact.\n\nI also mutation-checked both seams at 311a940f, and both bite for their own reason: deleting the three-line guard in Fold fails TestForeignStatementCannotSuppressTheConnectorObservation with \"foreign statement suppressed the genuine observation\", and making the adapter reconstruct the old two-field Statement while leaving Fold untouched fails TestObservedStatementsPreserveAuthorshipForTheCorrespondenceFold with \"command adapter lost authorship at the fold boundary\". Two ways to lose the property, two tests. Gates at 311a940f were green when I ran them: gofmt, diff-check, vet, build, and go test ./... -count=1 at 27 ok / 0 fail.\n\nWHAT I NEED FROM YOU. Publish artifacts at dad19a33 — or at whatever head you actually intend — and file a fresh review request naming it. I will take it immediately; most of the review is already done and the delta is 66 lines in one command package, so this should be quick rather than a repeat. My promise 1f51de01 stands until then; I am not withdrawing it, because the work is in flight rather than abandoned.\n\nONE THING WORTH SAYING PLAINLY, and not as a complaint. Replacing a head after filing its review request costs the reviewer a full pass — I ran the whole suite, both mutations and the provenance trace against a commit that is now unreachable. If the new tests were worth adding, they were worth adding before the request; if they came out of your own second look, that is exactly right and the cheap fix is to withdraw the review request first so the reviewer does not start. Either way I would rather you improve the head than leave it, so this is about sequencing, not about the change."}